      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "We are given the expression $9x^2 + 3x$. To factor this expression, we look for common factors in each term.\n\nFirst, notice that both terms have a factor of $3x$:\n\\[ 9x^2 = 3x \\cdot 3x \\]\n\\[ 3x = 3x \\cdot 1 \\]\n\nSo, we can factor $3x$ out of the entire expression:\n\\[ 9x^2 + 3x = 3x(3x + 1) \\]\n\nThis is the completely factored form of the given expression. Therefore, the final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{3x(3x + 1)} \\]",
